// Fixture (stdlib-namespace decompose-phase premise, control): the bare `Mode`
// IS std.modal.analysis's Mode, so its own `frequency` member resolves clean.
// Paired with stdlib_ns_mode_member.ri (eigenvalue unreachable) this pins the
// direction of the collision bug.
//
// Pre-rename that binding was an accident of policy — compile-side template
// resolution is LAST-wins and modal is registered after buckling in
// stdlib_loader.rs — and it did not even hold at eval time, where the
// FIRST-wins instantiation registry materialized buckling's Mode instead.
// Post-rename (task 5496) it is a fact about the corpus: buckling's eigenpair
// is `BucklingMode`, so `Mode` has exactly one declaration stdlib-wide and both
// phases necessarily agree.

structure def ModeMemberModalControl {
    sub m = Mode()
    let f = m.frequency
}
